---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../config';
---

<BaseLayout
  searchType="Pages"
  title={`About | ${SITE_NAME}`}
  description="What Samvidhan is, how it is built, how it stays current, and why it costs nothing to run."
>
  <div class="container page">
    <p class="kicker">About</p>
    <h1>{SITE_NAME}, the Constitution made readable</h1>

    <p>
      {SITE_NAME} is an independent civic project, not a government website. It presents the current text of the Constitution
      of India as readable, searchable pages: all 504 articles, 26 parts, 12 schedules, a timeline of all 106 amendments,
      and a tracker of amendment bills before Parliament.
    </p>

    <h2>Where the text comes from</h2>
    <p>
      The Constitution text is taken from the official Legislative Department edition, as on 1 May 2026. Statutes are
      public domain under Indian law, so the text is reproduced in full and never altered. Plain words summaries are
      original editorial content, labeled as summaries on every article page. See
      <a href="/sources/">sources and licensing</a> for the full list.
    </p>

    <h2>How it stays honest about age</h2>
    <p>
      There is no live feed of amendments or bills, so every fact carries the date it was verified. The footer records
      the verification dates for the text, the amendment list, and the bill tracker, and each bill row shows its own
      last verified date. A monthly update ritual refreshes them; the
      <a href="/changes/upcoming/">upcoming changes page</a> explains the pending bills in plain words.
    </p>

    <h2>How it runs</h2>
    <p>
      The site is fully static. Search runs in your browser, hosting is free, and nothing about your visit is tracked or
      sold. It works without JavaScript for reading: every article is complete in the HTML itself.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page {
    padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-4) var(--space-16);
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .kicker {
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-size: var(--text-body-s);
    color: var(--color-navy);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-display-l);
    color: var(--color-navy);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-heading-m);
    color: var(--color-navy);
    margin: var(--space-8) 0 var(--space-3);
  }

  p {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  a {
    color: var(--color-link);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
</style>
